--
--   Description
----------------
--
-- This checks PFC pause frame priority enable and the pause counters.
--
--
-- Functional Coverage
----------------------
-- This checks that the 8 PFC counters can decrement concurrently and will be
-- indepentdently updated of new PFC pause frames. Each counter is always loaded
-- on reception of a non-zero PFC frame when priority enable is set, and cleared 
-- on reception of a zero PFC frame. When priority enable is zero, the counter 
-- value is zero independent of the pause time value set in the PFC frame.
-- rx_pfc_paused[7:0] outputs are monitored when the counter is loaded 
-- and when the counter decrements to zero.Interrupt status bit is checked (that
-- it is not set) when timeout occurs.
-- Priority enable, loading counter with zero for zero pause frame and loading counters
-- with diffrent pause time value are checked in 'debug fast mode' (retry test bit set to 1)
-- Only check that the 8 PFC counters can decrement concurrently and will be
-- indepentdently updated of new PFC pause frames for nibble mode at 100Mbits/s 
-- and gigabit mode.
-- 
--
-- Detailed Test Description
----------------------------
--
-- *************************************************************
-- **** Set to 'debug fast mode' (retry test bit set to 1) *****
-- *************************************************************
--
-- Receive 3 PFC multicast pause frames with priority enable = 0x00FF
-- with diffrent pause time value. New PFC frames are recieved when all the counters 
-- decrement to zero.
-- Check rx_pfc_paused[7:0] outputs, interrupt status
--
-- Receive PFC multicast pause frame with priority enable = 0x00FF
-- with large pause time value. A new zero PFC frame is recieved when all the counters 
-- are not zero.
-- Check counters are cleared when zero PFC frame is recieved.
--
-- Receive PFC multicast pause frame with priority enable = 0x0055
-- Check the counters associated with zero priority enable are zero when the PFC frame is 
-- received and the other counters are loaded with their pause time and decrements over time.
--
-- Receive PFC multicast pause frame with priority enable = 0x00aa
-- Check the counters associated with zero priority enable are zero when the PFC frame is 
-- received and the other counters are loaded with their pause time and decrements over time.
--
-- Receive PFC multicast pause frame with priority enable = 0x0000
-- Check all the counters are zero when the PFC frame is received.
--
-- Receive a non-zero PFC multicast pause frame with 0x00ff pause time for each priority
-- priority enable =0x00FF.
-- Check that all the counters are loaded with 0x00FF and decrements to zero.
--
--
-- ******************************************************
-- ******** Set to  nibble mode at 100Mbits/s ***********
-- ******************************************************
--
-- Receive a PFC multicast pause frame with priority enable = 0x00FF
-- with diffrent pause time value. 
-- Check rx_pfc_paused[7:0] outputs, interrupt status (counter decrements evry 128 rx_clk)
--
-- ******************************************************
-- ********        Set to gigabit mode          *********
-- ******************************************************
--
-- Receive a PFC multicast pause frame with priority enable = 0x00FF
-- with diffrent pause time value. 
-- Check rx_pfc_paused[7:0] outputs, interrupt status (counter decrements evry 64 rx_clk)
--
--
-- *************************************************************
-- **** Set to 'debug fast mode' (retry test bit set to 1) *****
-- *************************************************************
-- Receive a non-zero PFC multicast pause frame with max pause time9 (0xffff)for each priority
-- priority enable =0x00FF.
-- Check that all the counters are loaded with 0xFFFF and decrements to zero.
--
--
-- 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


-- Configuration Requirements ..
requires ext_fifo_interface 1
pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 speed 0 --  check reset state

-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register

-- this is the event count that will initialize the scaler for event counts. it will cause any future scaling to only scale
-- the counts after start_scale
start_scale

apbwr      00 0001000C  -- enable receive/transmit and PFC pause frame reception
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      88 12345678  -- specific address register 1 bottom
apbwr      8C 00001111  -- specific address register 1 top
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register

-- # Initialize the network configuration register
-- #   -eam      <1|0|random>, default = 0. This is external address matching
-- #   -duplex   <full|half|random>, default = random
-- #   -speed    <1g|100m|10m|random>, default = random
-- #   -jumbo    <1|0|random>, default = random. This wont affect the RX transactor below, but will automatically cause jumbos to be dropped.
-- #   -copy_all <1|0|random>, default = 0. If 0, ensure you initialize the dest_addr in the rx transactor to something that will match
-- #   -databus  <32|64|128|take_from_cfg|random>, default = random, bus <= config.  The max value is the value set in dma_bus_width in gem_defs.v
-- #   -rx_toe   <1|0|random>, default = 0. Enables RX TCP/IP checksum offload
-- #   -pcs_en   <1|0|random>, default = 0. Enables SGMII PCS
-- #   -pause_en <1|0|random>, default = 0. Enables pausing of transmission
-- #   -dont_copy_pause <1|0|random>, default = 0. Controls whether pause frames are copied
init_ncr -sgmii_en 0 -pcs_en 0 -retry_test 0 -copy_all 0 -duplex half -speed 100m -jumbo 0 -databus 32 -eam 0 -rx_toe 0 -pause_en 0 -dont_copy_pause 0 -multicast_hash 0 -unicast_hash 0

apbrd      20 00000000  -- check contents of the receive status register and trigger reception of frame


